Compare to Parallel World Lines
Metric Isoclines in Polar and Rectangular Coordinates
Consider the Polar to Rectangular Transformation
The transformation of interest converts from polar coordinates to rectangular coordinates .
Two Dimensional Space (Stationary Points)

Horizontal lines:  \begin{align}y&amp;=\text{constant}\\\Rightarrow  dy &amp;= 0\end{align}
Vertical Lines:  \begin{align}x&amp;=\text{constant}\\\Rightarrow dx&amp;=0\end{align}
Circles around the origin:  \begin{align}r&amp;=\text{constant}\\\Rightarrow  dr &amp;= 0\end{align}
Rays pointing from the center: \begin{align}\phi&amp;=\text{constant}\\\Rightarrow  d\phi &amp;= 0\end{align}

